                                    Background="{DynamicResource InfoSurfaceBrush}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource InfoBorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1">
                                <TextBlock Text="Arkive proves the Western package identity, reference skeleton, LOD sections/chunks, exact GPU/index/colour buffers, and vertex-bound cloth/morph dependencies against UModel and native package data. Edited GLB import detects either the proven same-topology deformation route or the topology-capable LOD0 replacement contract. Every accepted skinned edit must preserve the exact target skeleton and pass deterministic CPU-skinned stress poses, influence-distribution checks, and deformation bounds before native compilation; these safety poses do not claim to execute every game animation clip. Select two clean exports to compare their rigs or create a conservative Blender retarget workspace. Cross-rig work keeps the target armature untouched, reports weighted/core-bone coverage, and marks unresolved donor groups for manual fitting and weight painting—Arkive never collapses missing bones to ancestors automatically. Same-topology edits preserve active cloth bindings and external morph targets byte-for-byte. Topology replacements may change vertices, triangles, UVs and skin weights only when dependency analysis proves no active cloth mapping or morph delta uses the old vertex identity; null clothing placeholders are not treated as cloth. New bones, new material slots, authored GLB morph targets, and topology remapping of active cloth/morph data remain refused. Verified topology edits can be composed with checked textures and materials under Modified UPKs. Second-batch builds require native decode-back, isolated append-and-retarget proof, exact-object UModel export under the original physical filename, source identity, backup capacity, and an auditable variable-size deployment gate before Install mod is enabled."
